course: dictionary
lesson: 10225
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Toast can be a food, a thing you do to food, or a wish you say to someone. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right.
explain: «Porridge, toast, cereal and fruit give steady energy before sport.» Porridge and cereal are breakfast foods, so toast must be a food too: bread that has been browned by heat. Try the swap test: "porridge, bread browned by heat, cereal and fruit" still makes sense.
explain: «Chapulines are toasted grasshoppers with lime and chilli.» The word toasted comes from the verb to toast, which means to brown food with heat. The clue is that the food is cooked, not drunk or warmed by a fire.
fact: Toast means bread whose sides have been made brown and crisp by heating.
fact: To toast food means to brown it with heat, so «toasted» means browned with heat.
fact: A toast is when people lift their glasses and drink to wish someone happiness or success.
fact: Toasting bread is a chemical change: the bread browns and cannot become untoasted.
fact: Never put a knife or fork in a toaster while it is plugged in.
exercise: «Porridge, toast, cereal and fruit give steady energy before sport.» In this sentence, what is toast? | *Bread that has been browned by heat | A type of cereal | To warm yourself by a fire | A drink that people lift to wish someone well
exercise: Ruby says, "Let's make a toast to Grandma!" What does a toast mean here? | Sitting by the fire to warm up | *Lifting glasses and drinking to wish Grandma happiness | To brown bread with heat | A slice of bread at breakfast
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Chapulines are toasted grasshoppers with lime and chilli» that means browned with heat. | *toasted | markets | thousands | eaten
test: «At a sleepover in Kent, Leo-Ray burns the toast because at home staff always made it.» What does toast mean in this sentence? | *Bread browned by heat | To warm yourself by a fire | A type of sleepover game | A drink to a friend
test: What is the safe rule for using a toaster? | *Unplug it before you reach in | Use a fork to pull out toast while it is plugged in | Push a knife in while it is plugged in to get stuck bread out | Leave it on with no bread in it
exam: Lucy says «I'll toast the bread» and Tom says «Let's toast Lucy's new job!» Which pair of meanings is correct? | The first means to drink, the second means to brown bread | Both mean to heat food | *The first means to brown bread with heat, the second means to raise glasses and wish her success | Both mean to warm yourself by a fire
